.TH CURTSY 1 "August 2026" "curtsy 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
curtsy \- transparent TCP and UDP traffic forwarder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B curtsy
.B --config
.I PATH
[
.B --check-config
]
.br
.B curtsy
.B --version
.br
.B curtsy
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B curtsy
is a Linux TCP and UDP traffic forwarder. It listens on one configured address
and port and forwards traffic to one configured upstream without terminating
TLS or inspecting forwarded payloads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c ", " --config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the YAML configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the configuration and resolved endpoints, then exit. Configuration
errors are reported on standard error and use exit status 2.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration. Invalid configuration or bind failures leave the
running configuration unchanged.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop accepting new connections and exit gracefully. Existing TCP connections
are allowed to drain until the configured shutdown grace period expires.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/curtsy/config.yaml
Default configuration path used by the packaged systemd service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/curtsy.service
Packaged systemd service unit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration loading, validation, or address resolution failed.
.TP
.B 64
Command line usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
